  "notes": "Every sprite key. `group: env` + `scale: 2` keys (Z63) are the environment kit: size is SOURCE px (author at double size), shown at 1/scale; their final art is art/frames/env/<key>.png (art:pack, inbox art/inbox/<batch>/env/). `placeholder.shape` cube is an isometric block (h = block height in source px, mark door|window on the `face`). size [w,h] px, anchor [x,y] 0-1, frames, status placeholder|final. A placeholder block is drawn in code by src/render/placeholders.ts (grey only; functional colours for blood). Codex replaces keys with final art. v2 adds `figures` and `atlases` (the atlas contract in art/STYLE.md): animated survivors and zombies. Each atlas has a `scale` (1 or 2, default 1): its cells are figures.cell times scale, the feet anchor stays at the same fraction (0.5, 0.875), and the game draws a 2x sheet at half size so a figure keeps its world size. The old one-image survivor_*/zombie keys stay until the shared renderer (Z25) stops using them.",
